WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.600
JOHN: Good morning, Hank!

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:01.440
It's Tuesday.

00:00:01.440 --> 00:00:02.020
HANK: Good morning, John!

00:00:02.020 --> 00:00:02.720
JOHN: Ohhhh

00:00:02.720 --> 00:00:04.340
It's a surprise reunion video.

00:00:04.340 --> 00:00:05.360
Who would've guessed it?

00:00:05.360 --> 00:00:07.740
HANK: I- I would never- I didn't even know I was here.

00:00:07.740 --> 00:00:09.240
JOHN: Alright Hank, I have some questions for you.

00:00:09.240 --> 00:00:15.240
First question: How many potatoes did the average Irish person eat per day in 1844?

00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:17.500
HANK: Do you want me to guess or know for sure?

00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:18.420
JOHN: Yes. I want you to guess.

00:00:18.420 --> 00:00:21.360
HANK: I'm gonna say... six.

00:00:21.460 --> 00:00:22.260
JOHN: 45.

00:00:22.740 --> 00:00:23.400
HANK: Wait, what?

00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:27.580
JOHN: The average Irish person in 1844, man, woman, and child, average human

00:00:27.580 --> 00:00:30.560
ate nine pounds of potatoes per day.

00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:32.560
Hank, can you really grow potatoes on Mars?

00:00:32.560 --> 00:00:34.400
HANK: Not the way they did in the movie.

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:35.140
JOHN: Okay.

00:00:35.140 --> 00:00:36.400
HANK: But yes!

00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:37.120
Other ways.

00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:38.340
Do you want me to get into it?

00:00:38.340 --> 00:00:39.220
JOHN: A little bit.

00:00:39.220 --> 00:00:42.180
HANK: Aright, well, you got some serious problems with Martian soil.

00:00:42.220 --> 00:00:47.220
It's got perchlorate in it, which is a big, big issue cause that's toxic to humans and also plants.

00:00:47.220 --> 00:00:47.720
JOHN: Kay

00:00:47.720 --> 00:00:51.380
HANK: Uh, if you can get that out, if you can get some of the other bad stuff out

00:00:51.380 --> 00:00:55.000
and you can put in some good stuff, yeah, you can- you could grow potatoes on Martian soil.

00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:56.040
JOHN: Even without an atmosphere.

00:00:56.040 --> 00:00:57.860
HANK: Oh, no, you'd have to build a thing around it.

00:00:57.860 --> 00:00:59.040
JOHN: You'd have to build an atmosphere.

00:00:59.040 --> 00:00:59.720
HANK: Yeah.

00:01:00.540 --> 00:01:06.380
JOHN: Hank, did you know that potatoes were responsible for at least 25% of Europe's population growth between 1700 and 1900?

00:01:06.380 --> 00:01:07.760
HANK: Noticing a trend here.

00:01:07.760 --> 00:01:08.440
JOHN: What's the trend?

00:01:08.480 --> 00:01:12.640
HANK: Potatoes seems to be the trend in this question Tuesday video.

00:01:12.640 --> 00:01:15.580
JOHN: It's weird, I just got a lot of potato questions. I don't know why.

00:01:15.580 --> 00:01:16.700
HANK: I also didn't know that.

00:01:16.700 --> 00:01:20.160
Uh, fascinating and I bet there's a CrashCourse video.

00:01:20.160 --> 00:01:24.040
JOHN: There is! You can watch the Columbian Exchange Crash Course video currently on Hank's head!

00:01:24.040 --> 00:01:27.380
Okay Hank, if you could create anything with potatoes what would it be?

00:01:27.960 --> 00:01:32.160
HANK: A man. A fully... a sentient being.

00:01:32.700 --> 00:01:34.140
JOHN: Like Mr. Potato head?

00:01:34.140 --> 00:01:36.960
They already did that. They already did that, it's in Toy Story.

00:01:36.960 --> 00:01:39.500
HANK: I want him... I want him to be a thinking, feeling potato man.

00:01:39.500 --> 00:01:40.720
JOHN: Have you not seen Toy Story?

00:01:40.720 --> 00:01:42.340
Please name three potatoes.

00:01:42.600 --> 00:01:43.660
HANK: Um...

00:01:43.680 --> 00:01:44.720
The Russett...

00:01:44.720 --> 00:01:45.460
JOHN: Yup.

00:01:45.480 --> 00:01:46.200
HANK: The Purple

00:01:46.200 --> 00:01:46.960
JOHN: Yup.

00:01:46.960 --> 00:01:47.780
HANK: The...

00:01:50.060 --> 00:01:51.200
Goldie Hawn.

00:01:51.200 --> 00:01:52.860
JOHN: That's a good potato name!

00:01:52.860 --> 00:01:54.720
If they haven't done that, they should.

00:01:54.720 --> 00:01:55.600
HANK: Yeah, they should.

00:01:55.600 --> 00:01:57.520
JOHN: They should. Why isn't there a potato named after Goldie Hawn?

00:01:57.520 --> 00:01:58.980
She's an American treasure.

00:01:58.980 --> 00:02:02.920
Hank, can you rename one of your favorite books by replacing one word with "potato"?

00:02:02.920 --> 00:02:03.720
HANK: Red Potato.

00:02:03.760 --> 00:02:05.520
The Fault in Our Potatoes.

00:02:05.700 --> 00:02:07.380
The Lord of the Potatoes.

00:02:07.400 --> 00:02:08.320
JOHN: God, I hate that book.

00:02:08.940 --> 00:02:11.440
I mean both the Lord of the Flies and the Lord of the Potatoes.

00:02:11.440 --> 00:02:12.580
HANK: Oh, I was talking about The Lord of the Rings!

00:02:12.580 --> 00:02:16.240
JOHN: Ohh! I have to teach Lord of the Flies this year in Crash Course Literature

00:02:16.300 --> 00:02:19.900
and I just openly revile the book, so it's going to be very challenging.

00:02:19.900 --> 00:02:21.020
HANK: That will be very interesting.

00:02:21.020 --> 00:02:24.940
JOHN: I'm quite fond of, uhh, Their Eyes Were Watching Potatoes.

00:02:24.940 --> 00:02:28.420
This is a good question. Uh. Which of you has a better potato impression?

00:02:28.420 --> 00:02:31.940
[A Potatoey silence]

00:02:31.940 --> 00:02:34.140
JOHN: You know potatoes have eyes, just like humans.

00:02:34.140 --> 00:02:35.460
HANK: Not just like humans.

00:02:35.460 --> 00:02:36.160
JOHN: [Giggles]

00:02:36.160 --> 00:02:38.180
JOHN: Couple questions not related to potatoes, Hank.

00:02:38.180 --> 00:02:39.560
HANK: Aw Pshh fshh faa

00:02:39.560 --> 00:02:41.260
JOHN: Sorry to do that for you.

00:02:41.260 --> 00:02:42.960
HANK: I'm completely unprepared for this.

00:02:42.960 --> 00:02:45.580
JOHN: Uh... What's the opposite of potato?

00:02:45.580 --> 00:02:47.160
HANK: That, is a potato question.

00:02:47.160 --> 00:02:48.800
JOHN: Henry, do you know what the opposite of potato is?

00:02:48.800 --> 00:02:49.700
HENRY: Uh, no.

00:02:49.700 --> 00:02:52.860
HANK: The opposite of potato is the vacuum of space.

00:02:52.860 --> 00:02:55.720
JOHN: I was going to say that the opposite of potato is a boysenberry.

00:02:55.720 --> 00:03:00.560
Actual non-potato related question, Hank: Are you stressed about the presidential race?

00:03:00.800 --> 00:03:01.700
HANK: Oh God.

00:03:02.400 --> 00:03:03.140
Yes.

00:03:03.140 --> 00:03:04.580
JOHN: What is your favorite one direction song?

00:03:04.580 --> 00:03:06.560
HENRY: My favorite song is...

00:03:06.560 --> 00:03:07.140
JOHN: Yeah.

00:03:07.140 --> 00:03:09.100
HENRY: ...fallahallaboom.

00:03:09.100 --> 00:03:12.000
JOHN: Henry's favorite song is, uh, fallerallaboom

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:17.520
which is what he calls, uh, Bomfalleralla of the, uh, Swedish hip-hop song on The Fault in our Stars soundtrack.

00:03:17.520 --> 00:03:20.680
JOHN: Hank what do you prefer, Potato Pizza, or Pizza Potato?

00:03:21.480 --> 00:03:22.620
Hank: Potato Pizza.

00:03:22.620 --> 00:03:25.040
JOHN: I also like potato pizza, it's an old favorite of mine.

00:03:25.040 --> 00:03:26.580
Under-appreciated Pizza!

00:03:26.580 --> 00:03:28.500
HANK: Yeah! Actually, I've had a lot of good potato pizzas.

00:03:28.500 --> 00:03:31.320
In the western Montana fair, they have this thing called the 'tater pig'.

00:03:31.320 --> 00:03:34.640
A tater pig is just a hollowed out potato with a hot dog shoved in it.

00:03:34.640 --> 00:03:36.000
HANK: It's not very good!

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:38.860
JOHN: Alright Hank, thank you for participating in Question Tuesday!

00:03:38.860 --> 00:03:42.560
JOHN: Hank, I'll see you on Tuesday. Friday! Whatever.

